<title>ESTONIA: RADIO HEADLINES - JUNE 25.</title>
<headline>RADIO HEADLINES - JUNE 25.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>These were the main headlines from Estonia's Kuku radio news report on Wednesday at noon. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>- Prime Minister Mart Siimann unofficially met his Russian counterpart at the UN Conference in New York.</p>
<p>- Bonnier Group decided to buy the remaining 49 percent stake in Estonia's business newspaper Aripaev. When the deal is completed, Bonnier will hold 100 percent of Aripaev.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
